Feature: Session Write-Back
  As a specialist agent operator
  I want approved session artefacts and quality signals written to Graphiti after Coach acceptance
  So that future sessions compound on prior learnings via the knowledge graph

  Background:
    Given the Graphiti service is available
    And a role configuration exists for "architect" with knowledge_graph.write_back enabled
    And a project with identifier "finproxy"

  # ━━ GROUP A: Key Examples (5 scenarios) ━━

  # Why: Core write-back path — approved output triggers Graphiti writes with correct group IDs
  @key-example @smoke
  Scenario: Approved session writes artefacts to Graphiti with project group ID
    Given a greenfield session completes with a Coach score of 0.72
    And the session produced 2 ADRs and 1 preferred direction
    When the write-back step executes
    Then each ADR should be written as a separate Graphiti episode with group_id "finproxy"
    And the preferred direction should be written as a Graphiti episode with group_id "finproxy"

  # Why: Role-level quality signals enable cross-project compounding
  @key-example @smoke
  Scenario: Quality signals are written to the role-specific group ID
    Given a greenfield session completes successfully for role "architect"
    And the session used 3 iterations with scores 0.45, 0.58, and 0.72
    And 1 detection finding of type "SCOPE_CREEP" was recorded
    When the write-back step executes
    Then a quality signal episode should be written with group_id "role:architect"
    And the episode should contain the iteration count, score history, and detection types

  # Why: Only approved output gets written — rejected iterations are excluded
  @key-example @smoke
  Scenario: Only the final accepted output is written, not intermediate rejections
    Given a session that ran 3 iterations before acceptance
    When the write-back step executes
    Then only artefacts from the final accepted iteration should be written to Graphiti
    And no content from rejected iterations should appear in the knowledge graph

  # Why: Write-back integrates into existing session lifecycle without disrupting output
  @key-example
  Scenario: Write-back occurs after filesystem output is written
    Given a greenfield session completes with Coach acceptance
    When the session reaches the COMPLETE phase
    Then the conversation starter file should be written to the output directory first
    And the session log should be written second
    And the Graphiti write-back should execute third
    And the SessionResult should reflect all three operations

  # Why: Each role writes different artefact types as configured in role.yaml
  @key-example
  Scenario: Role configuration determines which artefact types are written
    Given a role configuration with write_artefacts including "adr", "pattern", and "quality_signal"
    When a session completes and write-back executes
    Then only the configured artefact types should be written to Graphiti
    And artefacts not listed in write_artefacts should be silently skipped

  # ━━ GROUP B: Boundary Conditions (4 scenarios) ━━

  # Why: Just-at-threshold — score exactly at pass_threshold should still trigger write-back
  # [ASSUMPTION: confidence=medium] Pass threshold is 0.6 based on existing SessionConfig default
  @boundary
  Scenario: Session at exactly the pass threshold triggers write-back
    Given a pass threshold of 0.6
    And a session completes with a final score of exactly 0.6
    When the COMPLETE phase runs
    Then the Graphiti write-back should execute

  # Why: Just-below-threshold — failed sessions must NOT write back
  @boundary @negative
  Scenario: Session below the pass threshold does not trigger write-back
    Given a pass threshold of 0.6
    And a session exhausts max iterations with a best score of 0.59
    When the COMPLETE phase runs
    Then no Graphiti write-back should occur
    And no episodes should be added to the knowledge graph

  # Why: Zero detection findings is a valid quality signal (means the role is improving)
  @boundary
  Scenario: Session with zero detection findings writes a clean quality signal
    Given a session completes successfully with no detection findings
    When the quality signal episode is written
    Then the episode should record zero detections and the iteration count
    And the detection_types field should be an empty list

  # Why: Session producing no extractable artefacts (e.g. no ADRs in output) should still write quality signals
  @boundary
  Scenario: Session with no extractable artefacts still writes quality signals
    Given a session completes successfully but no ADRs are found in the output
    When the write-back step executes
    Then zero ADR episodes should be written to the project group
    And a quality signal episode should still be written to the role group

  # ━━ GROUP C: Negative Cases (4 scenarios) ━━

  # Why: Graphiti unavailability must not crash the session or lose filesystem output
  # [ASSUMPTION: confidence=medium] Write-back failure does NOT change SessionResult.success
  @negative @smoke
  Scenario: Graphiti service unavailable does not fail the session
    Given the Graphiti service is unavailable
    And a session completes with Coach acceptance
    When the write-back step executes
    Then the filesystem output should already be written
    And the write-back should log a warning
    And the SessionResult should still indicate success
    And no exception should propagate to the caller

  # Why: Knowledge graph disabled in role config should skip write-back entirely
  @negative
  Scenario: Write-back is skipped when knowledge_graph is disabled in role config
    Given a role configuration with knowledge_graph.write_back set to false
    And a session completes with Coach acceptance
    When the COMPLETE phase runs
    Then no Graphiti episodes should be written
    And no Graphiti connection should be attempted

  # Why: Invalid group_id configuration should not write to incorrect scopes
  @negative
  Scenario: Missing project_id in session config prevents project-scoped writes
    Given a session configuration with no project identifier
    And a session completes with Coach acceptance
    When the write-back step executes
    Then role-scoped episodes should still be written with group_id "role:architect"
    And no project-scoped episodes should be written
    And a warning should be logged about the missing project identifier

  # Why: Partial write failure should not corrupt the knowledge graph
  @negative
  Scenario: Failure writing one episode does not prevent writing remaining episodes
    Given a session produced 2 ADRs and 1 quality signal
    And writing the first ADR episode to Graphiti fails
    When the write-back step continues
