    And the quality signal episode should still be attempted
    And the warning log should record which episodes failed

  # ━━ GROUP D: Edge Cases (4 scenarios) ━━

  # Why: Artefact content must stay within Graphiti's extraction limit
  # [ASSUMPTION: confidence=medium] Artefact content size limit is 8,192 tokens (nomic embedding model input limit)
  @edge-case
  Scenario: Large artefact content is truncated before writing to Graphiti
    Given a session produces an ADR whose text exceeds 8,192 tokens
    When the write-back step prepares the episode
    Then the episode content should be truncated to fit within the extraction limit
    And a warning should be logged about content truncation
    And the truncated episode should still be written

  # Why: Concurrent sessions on the same project must not produce duplicate episodes
  @edge-case
  Scenario: Write-back includes session ID to prevent duplicate episodes
    Given two sessions complete for project "finproxy" within the same minute
    When both sessions write ADR episodes to Graphiti
    Then each episode should include the session ID as metadata
    And the episodes should be distinguishable in the knowledge graph

  # Why: Fleet-wide patterns (from phaseG-scope.md) need correct group_id routing
  @edge-case
  Scenario: Patterns discovered during session are written to the role group, not fleet
    Given a session where the Coach identifies a high-scoring architectural pattern
    And the pattern scores above 0.8 on the relevant criterion
    When the write-back step executes
    Then the pattern should be written with group_id "role:architect"
    And the pattern should NOT be written to "appmilla-fleet"

  # Why: The write-back must be idempotent — re-running should not create duplicates
  # [ASSUMPTION: confidence=low] Idempotency via session ID + artefact type as deduplication key in episode metadata
  @edge-case
  Scenario: Re-running write-back for the same session does not create duplicate episodes
    Given a session has already written its artefacts to Graphiti
    When the write-back step is re-executed for the same session ID
    Then no duplicate episodes should be created
    And the existing episodes should remain unchanged

  # ━━ EXPANSION: Security (2 scenarios) ━━

  # Why: Player output could contain adversarial content that corrupts the knowledge graph
  @edge-case @security
  Scenario: Episode content with prompt injection patterns is sanitised before writing
    Given a session produces an ADR containing text that resembles LLM prompt injection
