    Then the project group_id should be the literal string "role:architect-attack"
    And the role group_id should remain "role:architect" from the role configuration
    And no episodes should be misrouted to the role scope via the project identifier

  # ━━ EXPANSION: Concurrency (2 scenarios) ━━

  # Why: Multiple sessions may complete simultaneously — writes must not block or corrupt
  @edge-case @concurrency
  Scenario: Write-back completes while Graphiti is processing another session's ingestion
    Given another session is concurrently writing episodes to Graphiti
    When this session's write-back step executes
    Then all episodes from this session should be written with correct group IDs
    And no episodes from the concurrent session should be affected

  # Why: User interruption during write-back must not leave orphaned partial state
  @edge-case @concurrency
  Scenario: Session interrupted during write-back does not leave corrupted state
    Given a session has written the filesystem output and session log
    And the write-back step has written 1 of 3 episodes to Graphiti
    When the process is interrupted
    Then the filesystem output should remain intact
    And the successfully written episode should remain valid in the knowledge graph
    And the unwritten episodes should simply be absent, not partially written

